§ `2018, c. 16, s. 190 -- subsection 737(1) (victim surcharge) replaced, if Bill C-28 receives royal assent`

-- 190 If Bill C-28 (victim surcharge) receives royal assent, then, on the first day on which both subsection 2(1) of that Act and section 222 of this Act are in force, subsection 737(1) of the Code is replaced by the following.
-- src:19517 | AMENDMENTS NOT IN FORCE
-- src:19520 | 190 If Bill C-28, introduced in the 1st session of the 42nd Parliament and entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (victim surcharge), receives royal assent, then, on the first day on which both subsection 2(1) of that Act and section 222 of this Act are in force, subsection 737(1) of the Criminal Code is replaced by the following:
@ref 2018, c. 16, s. 190 (src:19517-19520)
GIVEN `Bill C-28, introduced in the 1st session of the 42nd Parliament and entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (victim surcharge), receives royal assent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the first day on which both subsection 2(1) of that Act and section 222 of 2018, c. 16 are in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2018 c 16 s 190 subsection 737(1) is replaced by the following` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Bill C-28, introduced in the 1st session of the 42nd Parliament and entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (victim surcharge), receives royal assent` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If Bill C-28, introduced in the 1st session of the 42nd Parliament and entitled An Act to amend the Criminal Code (victim surcharge), receives royal assent"
        IF `it is the first day on which both subsection 2(1) of that Act and section 222 of 2018, c. 16 are in force` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the first day on which both subsection 2(1) of that Act and section 222 of this Act are in force"

-- 737 (1) [as replaced] Subject to subsection (1.1), an offender who is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an offence under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act
-- shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence, in addition to any other punishment imposed on the offender. Subsection (1.1) lies outside this part's range (it is in-force text that another part encodes): its answer is an input.
-- src:19521 | Victim surcharge
-- src:19522 | 737 (1) Subject to subsection (1.1), an offender who is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an offence under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence, in addition to any other punishment imposed on the offender.
@ref s 737(1) as replaced by 2018, c. 16, s. 190 (src:19521-19522)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence under the Criminal Code, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 737(1.1) subsection 737(1.1) relieves the offender of the surcharge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of the offence` AND `the offence is an offence under the Criminal Code, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offender who is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an offence under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act"
        IF `s 737(1.1) subsection 737(1.1) relieves the offender of the surcharge` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (1.1)"
        IF `s 737(1.1) subsection 737(1.1) relieves the offender of the surcharge` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (1.1) lies outside this part's range
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

