§ `2023, c. 28, s. 35 -- section 743.2 replaced: what the court forwards to the Correctional Service of Canada`

-- 743.2 [as replaced] A court that sentences or commits a person to penitentiary shall forward to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal,
-- any relevant reports that were submitted to the court, any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal and the name and contact information for any victim who wishes to receive information under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act.
-- src:19540 | 35 Section 743.2 of the Act is replaced by the following:
-- src:19541 | Report by court to Correctional Service
-- src:19542 | 743.2 A court that sentences or commits a person to penitentiary shall forward to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal, any relevant reports that were submitted to the court, any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal and the name and contact information for any victim who wishes to receive information under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act.
@ref s 743.2 as replaced by 2023, c. 28, s. 35 (src:19540-19542)
DECLARE `s 743.2 (not in force) what the court forwards` IS ONE OF
    `s 743.2 (not in force) its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal`
    `s 743.2 (not in force) any relevant reports that were submitted to the court`
    `s 743.2 (not in force) any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal`
    `s 743.2 (not in force) the name and contact information for any victim who wishes to receive information under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`
    `s 743.2 (not in force) something else`

@ref s 743.2 as replaced by 2023, c. 28, s. 35 (src:19540-19542)
GIVEN `the court sentences or commits a person to penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `s 743.2 (not in force) what the court forwards`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 743.2 (not in force) the court shall forward the item to the Correctional Service of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court sentences or commits a person to penitentiary` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that sentences or commits a person to penitentiary"
        IF item EQUALS `s 743.2 (not in force) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall forward to the Correctional Service of Canada" names what the court forwards and does not say it forwards nothing else
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 743.2 (not in force) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 743.2 (not in force) forward to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal, any relevant reports that were submitted to the court, any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal and the name and contact information for any victim who wishes to receive information under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`

@ref s 743.2 as replaced by 2023, c. 28, s. 35 (src:19540-19542)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 743.2 (not in force) act`
`s 743.2 (not in force) the court must forward the reasons, reports, information and victim contact details to the Correctional Service of Canada` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 743.2 (not in force) forward to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal, any relevant reports that were submitted to the court, any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal and the name and contact information for any victim who wishes to receive information under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "a court that sentenced or committed a person to penitentiary did not forward to the Correctional Service of Canada what section 743.2 requires"

§ `2024, c. 33, s. 2 -- subsection 679(7) replaced: release or detention pending a miscarriage of justice review`

-- 679 (7) [as replaced] If the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission notifies a person under 696.4(5) that their application for review is admissible, this section applies to the release or detention of that person
-- as though that person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a), pending the completion of the review, pending a new trial or hearing directed by the Commission or pending the hearing and determination of a matter referred by the Commission to the court of appeal.
-- src:19545 | 2 Subsection 679(7) of the Criminal Code is replaced by the following:
-- src:19546 | Release or detention — miscarriage of justice review
-- src:19547 | (7) If the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) notifies a person under subsection 696.4(5) that their application for review is admissible, this section applies to the release or detention of that person — as though that person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a) — pending the completion of the review, pending a new trial or hearing directed by the Commission or pending the hearing and determination of a matter referred by the Commission to the court of appeal.
@ref s 679(7) as replaced by 2024, c. 33, s. 2 (src:19545-19547)
DECLARE `s 679(7) (not in force) the time` IS ONE OF
    `s 679(7) (not in force) pending the completion of the review`
    `s 679(7) (not in force) pending a new trial or hearing directed by the Commission`
    `s 679(7) (not in force) pending the hearing and determination of a matter referred by the Commission to the court of appeal`
    `s 679(7) (not in force) at some other time`

@ref s 679(7) as replaced by 2024, c. 33, s. 2 (src:19545-19547)
GIVEN `the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) has notified the person under subsection 696.4(5) that their application for review is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
      time IS A `s 679(7) (not in force) the time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(7) (not in force) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) has notified the person under subsection 696.4(5) that their application for review is admissible` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1) notifies a person under subsection 696.4(5) that their application for review is admissible"
        IF time EQUALS `s 679(7) (not in force) at some other time` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "pending the completion of the review, pending a new trial or hearing directed by the Commission or pending the hearing and determination of a matter referred by the Commission to the court of appeal"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
